# Line-ending policy.
#
# Every commit was emitting "LF will be replaced by CRLF" warnings because there was
# no policy here, leaving normalisation to each contributor's core.autocrlf setting.
# A contributor with autocrlf=false commits CRLF and produces a whole-file diff on a
# file nobody meaningfully changed.
#
# text=auto eol=lf stores LF in the index AND checks out LF, regardless of local
# config or platform. LF in the working tree also matters because CI runs on Linux:
# a Python or shell script checked out with CRLF line endings fails there on the
# shebang. The project now supports Windows contributors explicitly, so this needs
# to be settled by the repo, not by each machine.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets: never diff, never normalise line endings.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.docx  binary
*.pptx  binary
*.xlsx  binary

# SVG is XML, so it stays text and benefits from real diffs.
*.svg   text eol=lf
